{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454547-a-question-of-scale","id":1454547,"title":"A Question of Scale","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-08T14:12:33-07:00","id":1454547,"title":"A Question of Scale","content":"Equipment scale confuses me in the books. So looking at the books an anti-personal rifle is scale 3 for power. Then you have in the core the assault rifle. So is that a scale 3 weapon if I fire it into a fleshy person who is only scale 1? Is tactical armor itself also a scale 3 durability on top of its normal bonuses so someone trying to punch someone in that kind of armor has the scale issues to get past on top of the other armor bonuses it provides? How does a laser carbine for scale compare with an assault rifle? Also the description on what scale you can effect on page 112 seems to be in contradiction. Can you not effect something 3 or more scale above you or just no greater than 3.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/BogMod\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/BogMod</a> I play a lot of videogames.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/131-bogmod","name":"BogMod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-08T14:56:12-07:00","id":1454551,"title":"","content":"This questions come to forum once in a while. Do you mind to check this other post? Maybe it can help you to get the impacts of scale in combat.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1453553-is-scale-on-weapons-set-by-tags-or-by-narrative-description\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ve-description</a><br /> <br /> On the limits of overwhelming scale, yes, there are a few times it is mentioned and it has this contradiction. My suggestion is 3+ and not more than 3, but if you want to play all the way, 6 enhancements is basically the same as \u201cyou win\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 07-08-2021, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-13T04:50:06-07:00","id":1454811,"title":"","content":"As far as I can tell, they decided to have detailed Weapons rules that didn't generally use Scale, then separately use real-life weapons as a shorthand way to describe example Scales without meaning that the weapons within the game actually have Scale. It's needlessly confusing and also means that the official weapon stats are significantly weaker than what a different part of the game implies those weapons should be able to do.<br /> <br /> I want to say again that I really like Onyx Path games, even though I gripe about things like this. I just have no idea why every game has to be 99% awesome mixed with 1% incredibly confusing and self-contradictory stuff. (I mean, I know why. They get different people to write different sections, usually. Or the different sections are written at very different times, such as the Scale chart in Aberrant being finalized years after the weapons rules in Trinity Core.)<br /> <br /> My recommendation would be to either use the Weapons rules as-is and ignore the Scale table when it comes to how they work (this seems to be the official rule), or else ignore the complicated Weapons rules and instead just use the Scale table for guidance on how much Scale you get when you attack with a rifle or rocket launcher (which is definitely a house rule, but can work and makes the Scale table make more sense.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}